1
00:00:03,975 --> 00:00:31,256
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when I was speaking about virtue and the mind, something I had thought of bringing up is, why is it that, this is to say, that virtue is a necessary precondition, like purification of virtue, not just some amount of virtue, but purification of virtue is a precondition for purification of citta, which is a precondition for purification of you.

2
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:41,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is it that you can't just take a random person off of the street and then tell them to abandon the five hindrances and purify their citta?

3
00:00:44,068 --> 00:00:56,360
[SPEAKER_00]: Just by telling them to do exactly what the Buddha said in the suttas, just to abandon greed and aversion in regard to the world, abandon covetousness.

4
00:00:57,501 --> 00:00:58,882
[SPEAKER_00]: Why wouldn't they be able to do that?

5
00:01:21,358 --> 00:01:28,062
[SPEAKER_02]: Because acting in certain ways, whether you recognize it or not, is accepting that.

6
00:01:28,303 --> 00:01:35,427
[SPEAKER_05]: But what will happen if, let's say, at that moment, they're not acting in any unwholesome way?

7
00:01:36,288 --> 00:01:44,874
[SPEAKER_05]: Like, for that moment, factually, they're kind of... they're not breaking any precepts, because they're sitting down in a room, not doing anything.

8
00:01:45,314 --> 00:01:47,355
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they're kind of in seclusion at that moment.

9
00:01:47,395 --> 00:01:49,637
[SPEAKER_00]: So, why would they fail?

10
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:55,312
[SPEAKER_03]: Do they lack a degree of self-transparency?

11
00:01:57,339 --> 00:02:03,481
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but that would be like a very broad... that wouldn't necessarily tell you, like, what do I do then?

12
00:02:03,961 --> 00:02:05,282
[SPEAKER_00]: How can I fix that?

13
00:02:05,302 --> 00:02:18,965
[SPEAKER_02]: You'd still be looking at objects, at stuff, at things that arise, and blaming them, or trying to solve the problem by replacing, getting more or less.

14
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:23,567
[SPEAKER_04]: Why would that... why is that a problem, first of all?

15
00:02:24,587 --> 00:02:26,908
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, because the problem is not with the things that arise.

16
00:02:27,348 --> 00:02:27,588
[SPEAKER_02]: Uh-huh.

17
00:02:28,269 --> 00:02:31,750
[SPEAKER_02]: And why that would be is because...

18
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:39,214
[SPEAKER_05]: But what if... what if they just decide, like, okay, no, I heard that... that the objects are not a problem, so I won't replace them anymore.

19
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:48,418
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, then, you might have the thought that if you have been cultivating the... your view, your attitude, let's say, towards your experience of

20
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:57,329
[SPEAKER_02]: Getting rid of the stuff that bothers me and getting the stuff that satisfies me is beneficial.

21
00:02:59,111 --> 00:03:01,233
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't decide not to have that activity.

22
00:03:01,253 --> 00:03:06,960
[SPEAKER_02]: You have to undo it and it's going to take a while and as soon as you stop

23
00:03:08,683 --> 00:03:15,625
[SPEAKER_02]: That everything that you were doing before was secondary.

24
00:03:16,225 --> 00:03:16,566
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

25
00:03:16,866 --> 00:03:18,726
[SPEAKER_02]: And also how dependent on it you are.

26
00:03:20,087 --> 00:03:21,987
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, yeah, that's the point, because it's...

27
00:03:24,268 --> 00:03:33,975
[SPEAKER_05]: Because, you know, you might think like, okay, so, obviously, the focusing on objects is wrong, not replacing the one thing with another.

28
00:03:34,015 --> 00:03:37,157
[SPEAKER_05]: That's the basic self-transparency.

29
00:03:37,177 --> 00:03:39,238
[SPEAKER_05]: You realize that's only going to be a temporary solution.

30
00:03:40,619 --> 00:03:45,863
[SPEAKER_05]: But it goes much deeper than just not having heard that right information.

31
00:03:46,803 --> 00:03:53,448
[SPEAKER_05]: It's because even if you get the right information of, oh, I shouldn't be replacing things, I should be enduring them on the right level, quote-unquote,

32
00:03:54,347 --> 00:04:04,542
[SPEAKER_05]: That entire project is going to still be rooted, to some extent, in the fact that you don't want to endure the pressure, because if you allow the pressure to come up...

33
00:04:05,811 --> 00:04:08,632
[SPEAKER_05]: You will do the things that you're used to do on account of it.

34
00:04:09,373 --> 00:04:18,937
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you won't be able to not act out of sensuality and get up and go out, leave you in seclusion, if a real sensual thought were to arise.

35
00:04:20,517 --> 00:04:23,558
[SPEAKER_00]: So, because you're just not used to...

36
00:04:23,799 --> 00:04:25,459
[SPEAKER_05]: The precepts, that's the point of precepts.

37
00:04:25,499 --> 00:04:33,242
[SPEAKER_05]: It's not a... not a... like, just keeping this external behavior independently of what's going on in your mind.

38
00:04:33,483 --> 00:04:33,883
[SPEAKER_05]: It's like...

39
00:04:34,643 --> 00:04:39,486
[SPEAKER_05]: The whole point of the precept is to train you, so that even if these things arise, you don't act out of them.

40
00:04:40,506 --> 00:05:01,977
[SPEAKER_05]: If you spend most of your day in a state of trance, not even allowing these things to come up, then even if you keep your virtue for 20 years, you haven't trained yourself, because the whole point was to... like, when the mind was aware of these things,

41
00:05:02,517 --> 00:05:04,538
[SPEAKER_05]: Training it not to go for them automatically.

42
00:05:05,479 --> 00:05:17,165
[SPEAKER_05]: And so, only when that's in place, you will be able to train the wild animal, like the elephant, as we put it.

43
00:05:17,385 --> 00:05:24,569
[SPEAKER_04]: You will be able to... because, see, it's like the elephant hasn't even... you haven't even tied it down.

44
00:05:26,690 --> 00:05:27,610
[SPEAKER_04]: So, then, like...

45
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:29,511
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I was going to say, do you get

46
00:05:36,053 --> 00:05:37,854
[SPEAKER_01]: Even when the person is there.

47
00:05:57,547 --> 00:06:02,032
[SPEAKER_01]: In relation to that citta, which sits behind that, and which is putting the pressure there.

48
00:06:02,553 --> 00:06:09,220
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if those precepts are not adhered to from the start, you're not even gonna see that mind's pressuring you.

49
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,242
