50
00:06:12,643 --> 00:06:18,066
[SPEAKER_04]: Which is quite common, that the whole practice is supposed to prevent the pressure from coming up.

51
00:06:18,146 --> 00:06:29,773
[SPEAKER_04]: Because that's exactly the same thing, the same goal, because of which you act out of sensuality, act out of aversion, because you don't want to have the pressure.

52
00:06:30,353 --> 00:06:31,654
[SPEAKER_04]: So, anything you do,

53
00:06:33,022 --> 00:06:35,844
[SPEAKER_04]: Within that framework, we'll carry that same goal with it.

54
00:06:36,004 --> 00:06:39,707
[SPEAKER_04]: I don't want to hear my mind complaining.

55
00:06:40,547 --> 00:06:44,770
[SPEAKER_04]: So, I would just either give it what it wants, or just put it to sleep.

56
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:51,475
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and so, in the beginning, there's going to be a conflict, in a sense, between you wanting to keep the precepts, and your mind

57
00:06:53,096 --> 00:06:55,557
[SPEAKER_01]: Putting pressure on you, wanting to go the other way.

58
00:06:56,217 --> 00:07:00,540
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, there can be a natural inclination saying, look, I do not want to have that inner conflict.

59
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:07,544
[SPEAKER_01]: So, either you need to be stronger and tame the mind, or you're going to give in to the mind, in order to dissolve the conflict.

60
00:07:08,044 --> 00:07:10,685
