63
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:35,884
[SPEAKER_04]: So, it's essential to be self-honest about the fact that if you just look at something else and completely forget about that pressure, you're not dealing with the problem, even if temporarily you don't feel the pressure anymore.

64
00:07:35,904 --> 00:07:45,291
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the situation of suffering was pressure being present.

65
00:07:45,331 --> 00:07:47,213
[SPEAKER_04]: So, anything that you develop

66
00:07:48,763 --> 00:07:53,728
[SPEAKER_04]: Apart from that setup, it's completely irrelevant to what the problem actually was.

67
00:07:53,749 --> 00:07:53,989
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

68
00:07:57,805 --> 00:07:58,765
[SPEAKER_04]: It's like, yeah, I can...

69
00:07:58,925 --> 00:07:59,305
[SPEAKER_04]: I can...

70
00:08:00,185 --> 00:08:00,846
[SPEAKER_04]: I don't know, I can...

71
00:08:02,426 --> 00:08:05,947
[SPEAKER_04]: I can run when... when it's not uphill.

72
00:08:06,947 --> 00:08:09,907
[SPEAKER_04]: If it's uphill, I can't do it anymore.

73
00:08:10,047 --> 00:08:13,868
[SPEAKER_04]: And, like, the whole point is, the difficulty was, you couldn't run uphill.

74
00:08:14,728 --> 00:08:19,369
