75
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:21,370
[SPEAKER_04]: It doesn't matter.

76
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:28,612
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's the whole idea of meditation today.

77
00:08:28,872 --> 00:08:38,136
[SPEAKER_04]: It's based on that... just developing this huge... piling up this huge set of skills, put on boat.

78
00:08:39,367 --> 00:08:44,928
[SPEAKER_04]: In the domain that's completely separate from the problem that you were met with in the beginning.

79
00:08:44,948 --> 00:08:51,190
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the relationship between you and your mind, and who's now basically in charge of who.

80
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:52,050
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

81
00:08:52,250 --> 00:09:03,193
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you just... you're able to do all this stuff and have all this peace and stuff, because the things that provoke the mind are not there anymore.

82
00:09:05,388 --> 00:09:20,524
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, actually, the... like the... the point is... was to take that elephant and tame it, so that it would become a battle elephant, so that even when the... the... it would hear the drums,

83
