90
00:09:54,993 --> 00:10:00,755
[SPEAKER_05]: It's things that are... if the elephant is the citta, then the mind, then that's what these pressures are.

91
00:10:00,775 --> 00:10:09,518
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like those... the enemy trying to attack and get the elephant to run away or...

92
00:10:11,299 --> 00:10:11,600
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever.

93
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:15,168
[SPEAKER_00]: Just... just not do what it's... what you expect to do and put up with it.

94
00:10:15,188 --> 00:10:15,469
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

95
00:10:22,874 --> 00:10:30,858
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you miss... and you misascribe that, like, factual benefit of, like, the elephant not moving.

96
00:10:30,938 --> 00:10:46,165
[SPEAKER_03]: Or, say, you... you actually go higher up this hill, and you can see further, but it's because you've just been kind of running around, and you happen to climb higher, and you can see further, and you think it's because you've been running around and developing all these skills that you can see further.

97
00:10:46,305 --> 00:10:46,585
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

98
00:10:46,745 --> 00:10:50,146
[SPEAKER_03]: And, actually, it was just you... in your... Yeah.

