00:11:09,587 --> 00:11:12,089
[SPEAKER_04]: There is knowledge that can arise out of that, as they would say.

102
00:11:12,289 --> 00:11:14,571
[SPEAKER_04]: Out of wrong samādhi arises wrong knowledge.

103
00:11:15,271 --> 00:11:23,017
[SPEAKER_04]: But the knowledge will be on exactly the same level as the whole samādhi, and exactly on the same level as the whole wrong view of management.

104
00:11:24,038 --> 00:11:34,345
[SPEAKER_04]: So, all of those insights that you would see coming out of this, of that kind of practice of ignoring, which is what meditation is about for most people,

105
00:11:35,166 --> 00:11:55,126
[SPEAKER_04]: It would be about, like, yeah, you would hear, oh, everything is, as we were discussing in that previous talk, like, oh, everything is empty, it doesn't really exist, or it's all constantly changing, or you see the, the kind of, whatever, infinite, whatever, whatever infinite array of views you might come up with,

106
00:11:55,967 --> 00:12:02,772
[SPEAKER_04]: Just to justify yourself or to make yourself feel at ease with that pressure, because you don't want to put up with it.

107
00:12:03,593 --> 00:12:06,815
[SPEAKER_05]: You want to, to some extent, kind of dampen it.

108
00:12:06,855 --> 00:12:11,078
[SPEAKER_05]: You want to decrease it, because you have to convince the elephant.

109
00:12:11,098 --> 00:12:12,939
